# v0.5.0-rc.4 llama runtime for macOS arm64 (2026-10-11, release Mac): llama.cpp tag b10909 (commit
# a2878d30df0130dde503a7d9ba30d3d21bd71b9f) built from source with upstream's macos-arm64 release
# options (GGML_METAL_EMBED_LIBRARY, deployment target 13.3, @loader_path rpath, BoringSSL, RPC,
# tools + server, no tests/examples) plus -DLLAMA_BUILD_WEBUI=OFF -DLLAMA_USE_PREBUILT_UI=OFF, so
# llama-server embeds no web UI (0 assets; at b10909 LLAMA_BUILD_WEBUI alone still downloads the
# prebuilt UI). CPU probes pinned to the upstream M1 runner's result (dotprod, no i8mm/SVE/SME) so
# it runs on every Apple Silicon Mac. Developer ID signed (hardened runtime, timestamp).
# The tarball is the flat dependency closure of llama-server (11 Mach-O files, LICENSE-llama.cpp.txt
# and llama-server.sha256); the sidecar is the same llama-server with the extra rpath
# @loader_path/../Resources/llama. Replaces llama-server-aarch64-apple-darwin (ff931bc3..., b10909
# upstream with the web UI), which stays on runtime-deps unpinned.
